## Install

```bash
uv tool install {{project_slug}}    # or: pipx install {{project_slug}}
```

From a checkout, `make build` writes the wheel to `dist/`, and `uv tool install dist/*.whl` installs it.

## Usage

```bash
{{project_slug}} --help
{{project_slug}} --version
{{project_slug}} --json config show
```

<!-- stacks:fill The two or three commands people run most, with one line each on what they do. -->

Global options (`--json`, `--config`, `--verbose`, `--no-color`) go before the command. See [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md) for the config file, environment variables and exit codes.

## Development

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and make.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make install` | Create `.venv` and install the project and its dev tools |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check / fix lint and formatting (ruff) |
| `make typecheck` | mypy strict |
| `make test` | pytest, including tests that run the installed command |
| `make coverage` | Tests with the coverage floor |
| `make build` | Build the wheel and sdist and check their metadata |
| `make smoke` | Install the wheel in a throwaway environment and run it |

Run `make help` for the full list. [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) maps the modules.

